# Minor Blues in A (repertoire plan: st-minor-blues-a). An original study on the 12-bar form in
# minor: Am7 Am7 Am7 Am7 | Dm7 Dm7 Am7 Am7 | E7 Dm7 Am7 E7, straight eighths, played twice; the
# second time the last bar turns to Am7 to end.
# Melody: A minor pentatonic box 1 only (frets 5 to 8: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 3 on fret 7,
# finger 4 on fret 8), in three 4-bar lines like a sung blues: a line over Am7, the same idea a
# step higher over Dm7, and an answer over the turnaround. Every strong beat is a chord tone, or a
# step away from one. Over E7 the melody leans on E and D, the notes the box shares with the chord.
# Rhythm guitar: Am7 (x02010), Dm7 (xx0211), E7 (020100), down, down-up, down, down-up.
